{
	title: 'Clickable URLs in web questions',
	spec: 'Web question text displays bare HTTP(S) URLs as native underlined links, opening a new tab with noopener noreferrer so the pending form stays available. Preserve plain question text rather than interpreting Markdown or HTML; OAuth query parameters, percent escapes, and fragments remain intact. Sentence punctuation and unmatched closing parentheses are not part of the destination; non-HTTP(S) schemes remain inert. Long URLs wrap within the question at phone and desktop widths. Links keep the question colour and support native click, modifier-click, copy-link and keyboard activation; web forms use native Tab navigation across links and controls without submitting when Enter activates a link. Terminal rendering and authentication protocol are unchanged.',
